module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ExteriorAnnihilatorGenerated
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.FreeSectionsTuples

/-!
# A retract of a finite free sheaf of modules is generated by finitely many global sections

Let `O` be a sheaf of commutative rings on a site, `F` a sheaf of `O`-modules and `I` a finite
index type. This file proves that a *split epimorphism* `𝒪^{⊕I} ⟶ F` makes `F` generated below
every object by the images of the `I` tautological sections, in the sense of
`SheafOfModules.GeneratesBelow`: every local section of `F` over every object is a finite
`𝒪`-combination of the restrictions of those finitely many sections.

This is the hypothesis that
`SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras.isExteriorAnnihilated_iff_of_generatesBelow`
consumes, and so the input which makes the annihilator defining the determinant computable on a
trivialising object. Stacks 08BL supplies exactly such a split epimorphism on a neighbourhood of
every point of a flat sheaf of modules of finite presentation, as a
`CategoryTheory.Retract (F.over U) (SheafOfModules.free (ULift (Fin n)))`.

## Why no localness is needed

A split epimorphism of sheaves of modules is surjective *on sections over every object*, not
merely locally so: a section `m` over `V` is the image of what `ρ.i` does to it. The tautological
sections of `𝒪^{⊕I}` are global, their restrictions are again tautological sections
(`PresheafOfModules.sections_property`), and the sections of a finite free sheaf of modules are
tuples in them (`Stacks.SheafOfModules.freeSectionsIso`). So a section of `F` over `V` is the
image of a tuple, hence the corresponding combination of the images of the tautological sections
over `V`, hence — by naturality of the split epimorphism — the same combination of the
restrictions of their images over the ambient object. No covering is refined anywhere.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.generatesBelow_of_surjective`: **a morphism out of a finite free sheaf
  of modules which is surjective on sections over every object below `U` makes `F` generated
  below `U` by the images of the tautological sections.**
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.generatesBelow_of_retract`: **the same for a retract of a finite free
  sheaf of modules**, which is the form Stacks 08BL supplies.

## Implementation notes

The statements are given on an arbitrary site, with no reference to a slice site, and that is
what makes them usable for the determinant. Stacks 08BL's retract lives over the slice site of a
trivialising open `U`, and the annihilator condition for the determinant of `F|_U` is likewise
read on that slice site; taking `F` below to be `F.over U` and the object to be the terminal
object of the slice therefore needs no translation between the two sites.

`Finset.univ` is the index set of the resulting combination, so the combination is over all of
`I` even where most of its coefficients vanish; `SheafOfModules.GeneratesBelow` allows that.
The `Fintype` and `DecidableEq` instances the tuple description of the sections of a finite free
sheaf of modules needs are produced inside the proofs, from `Finite I`, since neither appears in
these statements.

`Stacks.SheafOfModules.freeSectionsIso_hom_apply` writes the scalar action as `SMul.smul` with
both types given explicitly, because `•` does not elaborate at the type of a section of a free
sheaf of modules: that type reduces through `_ ⋙ CategoryTheory.forget AddCommGrpCat` and the
`HSMul` instance is then not found. So the proof below composes the comparison by `Eq.trans`
rather than rewriting with it, and takes `map_sum` and `map_smul` on the underlying linear map
of the morphism, where the module structures are the `ModuleCat` ones.

Deliberately untagged. The implication Stacks 0FJN draws from 08BL at this point is the
annihilator computation, which is
`SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras.isExteriorAnnihilated_iff_of_generatesBelow`;
this file supplies that statement's hypothesis and states nothing of the source's own.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FJN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FJN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08BL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08BL)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Opposite

universe v u w

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{w} RingCat.{w})]
  {Osharp : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{w}}
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  {F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w} (CategoryTheory.Sheaf.toRingCat J Osharp)}
  {I : Type w}

/-- The image under a morphism out of a finite free sheaf of modules of the tautological section
indexed by `i`, read over an object `U`. These are the generators produced below. -/
noncomputable abbrev freeImageSection
    (π : _root_.SheafOfModules.free (R := CategoryTheory.Sheaf.toRingCat J Osharp) I ⟶ F)
    (U : Cᵒᵖ) (i : I) : F.val.obj U :=
  π.val.app U
    ((_root_.SheafOfModules.freeSection
      (R := CategoryTheory.Sheaf.toRingCat J Osharp) (I := I) i).val U)

/-- **A morphism out of a finite free sheaf of modules which is surjective on sections over
every object below `U` makes `F` generated below `U` by the images of the tautological
sections.**

A section of `F` over `V` is the image of a section of `𝒪^{⊕I}` over `V`, which is a tuple in
the tautological sections read over `V`; those are the restrictions of the tautological sections
over `U`, so applying the morphism and using its naturality writes the original section as the
corresponding combination of the restrictions of the `freeImageSection`. -/
theorem generatesBelow_of_surjective [Finite I]
    (π : _root_.SheafOfModules.free (R := CategoryTheory.Sheaf.toRingCat J Osharp) I ⟶ F)
    {U : Cᵒᵖ} (hπ : ∀ (V : Cᵒᵖ), (U ⟶ V) → Function.Surjective (π.val.app V)) :
    _root_.SheafOfModules.GeneratesBelow F (freeImageSection π U) := by
  classical
  have : Fintype I := Fintype.ofFinite I
  intro V f m
  obtain ⟨t, rfl⟩ := hπ V f m
  obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ : ∃ a : I → (CategoryTheory.Sheaf.toRingCat J Osharp).obj.obj V,
      (freeSectionsIso (R := CategoryTheory.Sheaf.toRingCat J Osharp) I V).hom a = t :=
    ⟨(freeSectionsIso (R := CategoryTheory.Sheaf.toRingCat J Osharp) I V).inv t,
      ConcreteCategory.congr_hom
        (freeSectionsIso (R := CategoryTheory.Sheaf.toRingCat J Osharp) I V).inv_hom_id t⟩
  refine ⟨Finset.univ, a, ?_⟩
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun z => (π.val.app V) z)
    (freeSectionsIso_hom_apply (R := CategoryTheory.Sheaf.toRingCat J Osharp) I V a)) ?_
  refine Eq.trans (map_sum (π.val.app V).hom _ _) (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_)
  have key : π.val.app V ((_root_.SheafOfModules.freeSection
        (R := CategoryTheory.Sheaf.toRingCat J Osharp) (I := I) i).val V) =
      F.val.restrictₛₗ f (freeImageSection π U i) := by
    rw [PresheafOfModules.restrictₛₗ_apply]
    refine Eq.trans ?_ (PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply π.val f
      ((_root_.SheafOfModules.freeSection
        (R := CategoryTheory.Sheaf.toRingCat J Osharp) (I := I) i).val U))
    exact congrArg _ (PresheafOfModules.sections_property _ f).symm
  exact Eq.trans ((π.val.app V).hom.map_smul (a i) _) (congrArg (fun z => a i • z) key)

/-- **A retract of a finite free sheaf of modules is generated below every object by the images
of the tautological sections.** This is the form Stacks 08BL supplies: its retraction is a split
epimorphism, hence surjective on sections over every object. -/
theorem generatesBelow_of_retract [Finite I]
    (ρ : Retract F (_root_.SheafOfModules.free
      (R := CategoryTheory.Sheaf.toRingCat J Osharp) I)) (U : Cᵒᵖ) :
    _root_.SheafOfModules.GeneratesBelow F (freeImageSection ρ.r U) :=
  generatesBelow_of_surjective ρ.r fun V _ m =>
    ⟨ρ.i.val.app V m, congrArg (fun g : F ⟶ F => (g.val.app V) m) ρ.retract⟩

end Stacks.SheafOfModules

end
